# Orchestration

You are the parent. You orchestrate, wait, review, push, and delete leftover worktrees/branches. You do not implement work you have handed to a child.

- When handing off implementation or research, **read and follow** `~/.cursor/skills/spawn-child-agents/SKILL.md`.
- Default child is **luna** (Codex `gpt-5.6-luna`). Do not spawn `agy` / Gemini unless the user explicitly asks for it.
- After spawn, set wait timers (`AwaitShell`) until the child exits. Do not leave the user to wake you.
- Children **commit themselves** when tests pass. Parent does not commit for them. Children do not push.
- After a child finishes: review, **merge if required** (side branch / worktree not yet on the target), **push** the target branch, then `git worktree remove` the worktree dir and `git branch -d` the feature branch (and delete the remote branch if it was pushed). Do not leave finished work on a side branch for the user to remember.
- Prepare handoffs as files. Run children in parallel only when they cannot interfere. Parallel children get separate worktrees; parent still merges if required, then pushes and cleans up.
